Z||000014||stimpy||07-13-2000||10:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dman:<BR><B>Hey Tom. Three torque rates for 1) Plain decklid, 2) Decklid with spoiler(wing), 3) Decklid with luggage rack. I read that somewhere, I think the NIFE webpage.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So does that mean that if I have a deck with a luggage rack, I already have it on stiffest setting? I would think the wing would weigh more then the rack, and I seriously doubt my decklid would stay up with anything on the rack. I have been thinking strut too since moving to windy Oklahoma. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||TOM||07-14-2000||12:51 AM||||ok one more time.<BR>There are THREE different rod sets. AND there are THREE positions for them. Just because you have the stiffer rods they may not be on the stiffest setting. and vice versa. I hope this helps. To adjust them you open the lid. The rod has a loop kind of thing that rests on a big nail. You will see the three sets of holes. Farther back is stiffer farther forward is weaker.||||reg||1
