Z||000027||Monkeyman||07-18-2000||12:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowCG:<BR><B>Thanks,for the info,full size,or S-10,do you recall?<BR>My car just got it's DOHC motor last week,haven't put the lid back on yet,and wasn't looking forward to not having a spring.<BR>Ok,I was just thinking how it has got to be the S-10,since I've never really seen a full-sized Blazer with anything but a window that disappears into the tailgate.<P>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 07-18-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The last generation of full size 2-door Blazers had a hatchback instead of the rear window dropping into the tail gate.  Also, the cap wasn't removable anymore.  (Good idea, IMO.  Once you remove the original cap and replace it, it's almost impossible to keep it from leaking either rain or wind.)<P><P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
